what does a valid signature prove? Three things:   
  Integrity the hashs need to match so it checks its the same and no changes
  Non repudiation - It was sent from that person they cant say it wasn't them
  Authentication - Only the private key could have made that signature as its checked by the public key (every one can see
  
Certificates
Self-signed certificate = “I’m a doctor, trust me.” Anyone can print their own degree at home. The value comes from a trusted third party vouching for you: the university for the doctor, the CA for the website. That’s exactly why browsers throw a big warning on self-signed certificates.

Authenticity.-  The message really came from the person who owns that private key.
Integrity. - The message hasn’t been changed since it was signed.
Non-repudiation. - The sender can’t later deny sending it, because only their private key could have produced that signature.

Remember for exam with this 
